  "description_short": "Authentic African cuisine in the heart of Plett, celebrating local flavours and traditional cooking methods.",
  "description_long": "Nguni Restaurant brings the rich culinary heritage of Africa to Plettenberg Bay's town centre. Named after the iconic indigenous cattle breed, this establishment honours traditional South African cooking with a menu that showcases local ingredients and time-honoured recipes. The warm, welcoming atmosphere reflects the spirit of ubuntu, making every meal feel like a homecoming.\n\nThe kitchen specializes in authentic African dishes that tell the story of the continent's diverse food culture. From hearty stews to flame-grilled meats, each plate is prepared with care and respect for tradition. The relaxed setting on Crescent Street makes it equally suitable for a casual lunch or a leisurely dinner with friends and family.\n\nConveniently located in central Plett, Nguni offers both dine-in service and takeaway options for those wanting to enjoy authentic African flavours at home or on the go.",
